Targets cover lifecycle/identity, source allocation, all byte/scalar partitions,
random longer partitions, malformed recovery/physical closers, explicit previews,
hard resources and soft allowances, adversarial complexity, typed views, and
existing semantic/artifact consumers. Full/base syntax --tests executes all new
targets. Reduced syntax CI names them explicitly; full_source CI includes the
canonical_document_streaming engine canary and the accumulated document-state
canaries. Runtime qualification also checks finalized streamed execution through
complete document rendering, plus resolver scopes, import spans, and grapheme
coordinates against one-shot documents. Native/WASM and generator/architecture
checks remain required. Pinned toolchain: nightly-2026-03-03, locked dependencies.

The committed s7b-streaming-qualification.json records all 68 measured growth
samples, the implementation commit, command, and focused pass counts. It
explicitly separates that result from the complete final-head matrix. Final CI
and review status must be confirmed on PR #826 before implementation closeout.
A queued job, zero-test feature-gated target, historical pass, or targeted subset
is not evidence that the complete matrix passed. Fix and respond to every relevant
review note before requesting another review. CI/review links and exact final
head results are published on that PR to avoid a self-referential commit hash.

8. S8 production handoff
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Allocate one DocumentStream per retained document and select hard limits.
   Buffer incomplete UTF-8 transport bytes outside the parser. Feed valid strings
   to append with a bounded allowance. Apply each update before driving advance
   again while NeedsProcessing.
2. Publish the returned journal deltas and shared views. Use full StreamIdentity
   as the cache key. Query completed_node for existing typed consumers. Offer
   preview only as an explicit finite-prefix operation with a provisional label.
3. Declare finish at the application's actual completion boundary. Drain work
   until Finished or Limited, applying every intermediate update. Cancellation
   and Limited do not authorize execution. Resynchronize after Limited export.
4. On Finished, materialize once and validate the canonical snapshot is strictly
   clean before passing its DocumentSyntax to the existing semantic frontend.
   Preserve the frontend's capability/semantic validation and artifact boundary.
   A clean finite preview is insufficient; require finalized lifecycle identity.
5. Select apply_edits or ownership transfer deliberately for editing. Invalidate
   caches using interpretation identity and deltas; do not reuse IDs from the old
   interpretation after a restart. Keep only needed historical views.
6. Migrate production input, rendering, and execution ownership in S8. Remove
   retiring ingestion/AST paths in that same migration, retain one canonical
   syntax authority, and run the accumulated native/WASM/consumer matrix.

Production caller switches, transport policy, semantic expansion, and scheduler
activation belong to S8 or their separately defined work. S7B hands off a retained
canonical syntax lifecycle with explicit progress, finality, resources and costs.

B6 accumulated-stack fixture qualification
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Full integration CI identified 17 source-compiled bytecode fixtures still carrying
graph revision 5 while the canonical decoder requires revision 6. The maintained
isolated producers regenerated the corpus. Section-by-section comparison proved
that only the graph revision and checksum changed: source text, expected output,
headers/section tables, all non-graph payloads, and all three constructed fixtures
remain identical. The manual corpus seals now cover those generated revision-six
artifacts. s7b-bytecode-corpus-migration.json records before/after hashes and the
comparison scope. No earlier graph reader or compatibility path was introduced.

B6 publication closeout qualification
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

document_streaming_publication applies every event/diagnostic suffix to an
application-owned mirror of shared journal ranges under allowance one, comparing the complete view after
every update, including cached-node identity. It covers speculative rewinds,
recovery, final EOF, edit restart, and explicit Limited export resynchronization.

The normal-view complexity path uses the same mirror and verifies its complete
final tape. The consumer preserves unaffected ranges from historical views,
trims/removes overlapping range descriptors, and adopts the new suffix as one
shared view/range. It charges descriptor visits, adopted/removed ranges, and update
applications. Logical removed record counts are separately reported; adoption
never enumerates those records. Full oracle scans are validation work, not normal
update operations. Diagnostic anchors bind lazily to the current revision.

A preliminary flat-vector consumer failed the 32-to-64 KiB generated-Mech gate:
738,035 to 2,262,698 record operations (3.066x), while combined work stayed below
3x. The qualified integration strategy therefore uses shared ranges, not repeated
suffix cloning. A concrete reference consumer is in tests/support/stream_mirror.rs.
This is existing StreamView sharing, with no acknowledgment or parser redesign.

The additional 8,192/16,384/32,768/65,536 size ladder includes generated Mech,
mixed Mechdown, unfinished strings/prose, executable fences, malformed tails,
and late brace selection. It uses 64-byte chunks and allowance 65,536, and gates
both combined work and consumer record work at at most 3x per doubling. Settled
prefixes separately gate a six-byte append across the same ladder. Explicit
limits: nesting 256, diagnostics 65,536, events 16,000,000, recovery bytes 8,000,000,
canonical fuel 1,000,000,000, retained bytes 1,000,000, session work 2,000,000,000.
Both one-shot and streaming outputs must remain uncapped and agree structurally,
diagnostically, and losslessly. These gates supplement the original small ladder;
they do not establish universal complexity or a measured speedup over S7A.

Finalized character streams also run the S7A Mika local/nested/named execution and
resolver owner checks. The CRLF fence-information accessor recognizes the
canonical CarriageReturn token (which retains the whole CRLF grapheme), preserving
configured scope/index behavior. Consumer paths reuse the same semantics.
Execution results for this candidate are recorded on PR #826 after validation.
